                  the second step is the definition of the classifying space (Def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassifyingSpaceAsShapeOfDelooping"}
              %li
                %p
                  the third step is the smooth Oka principle (Prop.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothOkaPrinciple"}
              %li
                %p
                  the fourth step is the relation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ʃ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Disc
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi Sing
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; \;\simeq\; Disc \circ Sing
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SmoothlyParameterizePathInfinityGroupoidIsDiscrete"} (5)
                  from Prop.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothShapeModelityGivenBySmoothPathInfinityGroupoid"}
              %li
                %p
                  the fifth step is the relation
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Pnts
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi Disc
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi id
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pnts \circ Disc \simeq id
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              %li
                %p
                  the sixth step is
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SimplicialFormulaForPathInfinityGroupoid"} (2)
                  from Def.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PathInfinityGroupoid"}
              %li
                %p
                  the seventh step is the formula for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                  by the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
              %li
                %p
                  the eighth step is the modulation of principal
                  = succeed "-bundles" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ModulationOfPrincipalInfinityBundles"} (8)
              %li
                %p
                  the ninth step uses that
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} n-truncation
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
                  and hence commutes with
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} (∞,1)-colimits
              %li
                %p
                  the tenth step uses that the inclusion of the first two face maps into the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+functor"} final functor
                  (by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "final+functor#FirstPairOfFaceMapsFinalInOppositeSimplexCategory"} this example
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} 0-truncated
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
              %li
                %p
                  the eleventh step invokes the definition
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SetOfConcordanceClassesOfPrincipalInfinityBundles"} (9)
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordance"} concordance
                  of principal
                  = succeed "-bundles" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConcordanceClassesOfPrincipalInfinityBundles"}
            %p
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordance"} concordance
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The identification in Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothShapeModelityGivenBySmoothPathInfinityGroupoid"}
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Pavlov14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Pavlov"}> Dmitri Pavlov
                \:
                %em Structured Brown representability via concordance
                (2014) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://dmitripavlov.org/concordance.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Pavlov_Concordance.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#BEBP19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Berwick-Evans"}> Daniel Berwick-Evans
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pedro+Boavida+de+Brito"} Pedro Boavida de Brito
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Pavlov"} Dmitri Pavlov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Classifying spaces of infinity-sheaves
                %strong 24
                (2024) 4891-4937 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2024.24.4891"}> doi:10.2140/agt.2024.24.4891
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.10544"} arXiv:1912.10544
          %p
            The special case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothShapeModelityGivenBySmoothPathInfinityGroupoid"}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"}
              smooth
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            (hence a
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
            of its shape
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \esh A
            was previously claimed (but see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/234778/381"} MO:q/234778
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ib+Madsen"}> Ib Madsen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Weiss"} Michael Weiss
              = succeed "," do
                %em The stable moduli space of Riemann surfaces: Mumford’s conjecture
              %strong 165
              3 (2007) 843–941 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212321"}> arXiv:math/0212321
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/http://doi.org/10.4007/annals.2007.165.843"} doi:10.4007/annals.2007.165.843
          %p
            while the “stable” situation, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is taken to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+object"} spectrum object
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"}
                smooth
                = succeed "-groupoids" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
              %strong 11
              1 (2016) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"}> arXiv:1311.3188
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40062-014-0092-5"} doi:10.1007/s40062-014-0092-5
          %p
            The particular conclusion
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ShapeEquivalentToDiscreteSmoothSingularComplex"} (6)
            is also claimed in:
          %ul
            %li#Bunk20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Severin+Bunk"}> Severin Bunk
              , Section 3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The
                  = succeed "-Local" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.06039"} arXiv:2007.06039
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40062-022-00318-7"} doi:10.1007/s40062-022-00318-7
          %p Another discussion is offered in:
          %ul
            %li#AmabelDebrayHaine21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Araminta+Amabel"}> Araminta Amabel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arun+Debray"} Arun Debray
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+J.+Haine"} Peter J. Haine
              (eds.), section 5 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential Cohomology: Categories, Characteristic Classes, and Connections
              %a{:href => "https://math.mit.edu/juvitop/pastseminars/2019_Fall.html"} Fall 2019 talks at MIT’s Juvitop seminar
              by: A. Amabel, D. Chua, A. Debray, S. Devalapurkar, D. Freed, P. Haine, M. Hopkins, G. Parker, C. Reid, and A. Zhang. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.12250"}> arXiv:2109.12250
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Yet an alternative proof of Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothShapeModelityGivenBySmoothPathInfinityGroupoid"}
            is also claimed in:
          %ul
            %li#Clough21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adrian+Clough"}> Adrian Clough
                , Theorem B of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Convenient Category for Geometric Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://repositories.lib.utexas.edu/bitstream/handle/2152/114981/CLOUGH-DISSERTATION-2021.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Clough-ConvenientCategory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adrian+Clough"}> Adrian Clough
                \:
                %em The homotopy theory of differentiable sheaves
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.01757"}> arXiv:2309.01757
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adrian+Clough"}> Adrian Clough
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The smooth Oka principle
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                (Oct 2022) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/adrianclough/adrianclough.github.io/raw/main/The%20smooth%20Oka%20principle%206.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The special case of the smooth path
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PathInfinityGroupoid"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            (among all
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoids"}
                smooth
                = succeed "-groupoids" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li#ChristensenWu13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Daniel+Christensen"}> J. Daniel Christensen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enxin+Wu"} Enxin Wu
              = succeed "," do
                %em The homotopy theory of diffeological spaces, I. Fibrant and cofibrant objects
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.6394"} arXiv:1311.6394
          %p
            Application of the theorem to a(n) (orbi-)smooth Oka principle (and coinage of that term) and to the classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+bundles"} equivariant
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
          %ul
            %li#SS21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Equivariant+principal+infinity-bundles"}
                    Equivariant principal
                    = succeed "-bundles" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.13654"} arXiv:2112.13654
        .revisedby
